## ZPE-XR — deterministic XR input-layer infrastructure

### (i) Best downstream wedge and why

**Best wedge: deterministic latent-action input layer for XR apps, anchored to Fanmode as first pilot customer.** The NeurIPS 2024/25 frontier has decisively moved from "record pixels" to "record latent actions + seeds + tokenized observations, replay via a world model." DIAMOND (Alonso et al., NeurIPS 2024 Spotlight, arXiv:2405.12399, OpenReview NadTwTODgC) shows an interactive CS:GO neural game engine is buildable **today** on consumer compute; Vista (Gao et al., NeurIPS 2024, arXiv:2405.17398) demonstrates 576×1024 action-conditioned driving rollouts; Genie / LAPO (Schmidt & Jiang, ICLR 2024, arXiv:2312.10812) proves **latent actions can be recovered unsupervised from video**, removing the need for ground-truth controller logs. This is the missing abstraction: ZPE-XR can ship a "latent-controller API" that makes any XR app replayable deterministically against a Cosmos-class world model without the app exposing raw input internals.

Rationale vs alternatives: a pure "XR video codec" wedge collides head-on with NVRC/DCVC-FM and is easily obsoleted; a pure "event-camera tokenizer" wedge is too hardware-specific. The latent-action input layer is the only wedge where the portfolio's deterministic-replay DNA maps to a NeurIPS-validated abstraction that nobody else has productized.

### (ii) Exact sequencing after Phase 09-02

1. Close the 0/5 public comparator — ship reconciled public repo with a minimal `xr-replay-core` crate exposing (observation_token, latent_action, seed) triples.
2. Integrate OmniTokenizer (Wang et al., NeurIPS 2024, arXiv:2406.09399) as the default observation tokenizer (1.11 rFID, 42 rFVD, joint image+video, window+causal attention) — this is industry-consistent and gives free cross-compatibility with Cosmos-Tokenizer-DV8x16x16 (NVIDIA, arXiv:2501.03575).
3. Add a LAPO-style latent-action head trained on Ego-Exo4D (Grauman et al., CVPR 2024, arXiv:2311.18259) + OpenXR controller traces; publish an 8–16 latent-action vocabulary.
4. Only after those three: Phase 10 Fanmode pilot, demonstrating deterministic session replay inside a DIAMOND-class diffusion engine.

### (iii) Strongest commercial and grant framing

**Commercial:** "Deterministic XR session recorder + latent-controller SDK" — primary customers Meta Reality Labs / Apple Vision / Microsoft Mesh XR QA teams who need replay for regression testing; secondary customers sim-to-real robotics teams (NVIDIA Isaac Lab, Unitree, 1X) who already need latent-action abstractions.

**Grant:** EU Digital Europe **DIGITAL-2026-AI-09 Virtual Worlds Testbeds STEP** (deadline 1 Oct 2026) is the single most direct thematic match; HE CL4 HORIZON-CL4-2026-04-HUMAN-02 Web 4.0 is secondary. US vehicle: NSF CISE Future CoRe (IIS HCI), next target Feb 2027 with Sep 2026 fallback. SA/APAC: TIA-TuksNovation Seed for Fanmode pilot; Korea IITP XR track.

### (iv) Minimal proof packet for the wedge

(a) 500 XR session recordings, each ≤30 s, across 3 Fanmode-style apps;
(b) OmniTokenizer-encoded observation stream at ≥50:1 compression vs raw H.264;
(c) LAPO latent-action head with ≥0.85 action-consistency on held-out sessions;
(d) 1-line public demo: "deterministic replay of recorded XR session in a DIAMOND-class world model";
(e) reproducibility harness with fixed seeds + pinned tokenizer weights.

### (v) Ranked 3-step action plan with hold conditions

1. **Close Phase 09-02 public comparator (0/5 → 5/5)**. Hold: if closure requires >4 weeks, re-scope comparator to a narrower 3-test subset and ship.
2. **Adopt OmniTokenizer + Cosmos-Tokenizer as observation tokenizer layer** (engineering complexity M). Hold: if OmniTokenizer rFVD on Ego-Exo4D test split >60 after finetune, fall back to Cosmos-CV8x8x8.
3. **Train LAPO-style latent-action head on Ego-Exo4D + OpenXR traces, release `xr-replay-core` crate**. Hold: if latent-action stability <0.70 on held-out Fanmode sessions, park the latent-action wedge and ship pure tokenized-observation replay instead.

**Kill condition:** if Phase 09-02 comparator cannot be stabilized in 6 weeks and Fanmode pilot LOI lapses, park ZPE-XR at Phase 10 and redirect capacity to ZPE-Video + ZPE-Bio (higher-gradient lanes).

### (vi) NeurIPS 2024/25 citations — one-line relevance

- **DIAMOND** (Alonso et al., NeurIPS 2024 Spotlight, arXiv:2405.12399, OpenReview NadTwTODgC) — continuous diffusion world model, direct substrate for deterministic XR replay.
- **Vista** (Gao et al., NeurIPS 2024, arXiv:2405.17398, OpenReview Tw9nfNyOMy) — multi-modal action-conditioned rollouts at 576×1024, template for controller→pixel pipeline.
- **OmniTokenizer** (Wang et al., NeurIPS 2024, arXiv:2406.09399, OpenReview H6C4p8Dir7) — joint image+video tokenizer, default XR observation encoder.
- **Overcoming Challenges of Long-Horizon Prediction in Driving World Models** (Mousakhan et al., NeurIPS 2025 Poster) — continuous AR beats discrete tokens on long horizons; re-scopes "tokenize-everything" XR prior.

### Re-scope argument against the current prior

The current brief implicitly treats XR as a standalone codec lane. NeurIPS 2024/25 evidence (DIAMOND + Vista + LAPO + Cosmos) argues XR should be re-scoped as **a deterministic-replay front-end to a world-model substrate**, with the codec being the observation-tokenizer layer that feeds world models. This is a strictly larger surface area and the only framing in which Fanmode is a natural first customer rather than an arbitrary one.

### Engineering augmentation (concrete build)

**Build:** `xr-replay-core` — a 3-crate stack (Rust): `xr-obs-tok` wrapping OmniTokenizer + Cosmos-Tokenizer; `xr-latent-act` wrapping a LAPO head; `xr-replay-harness` providing deterministic seed+token replay. **Why:** unlocks (i) EU Virtual Worlds Testbeds grant alignment, (ii) QA-tooling commercial wedge at Meta/Apple/Microsoft, (iii) cross-lane reuse — the same harness serves ZPE-Mocap (retarget replay) and ZPE-Neuro (deterministic neural-data replay). **Expected complexity:** M (~10 eng-weeks).

