## ZPE-Video — cross-writer hash-stable AI-perception receipts

### (i) Near-term wedge: receipt program vs primitive-native continuation

**Verdict: receipt program wins decisively.** NeurIPS 2024 evidence is unambiguous: **invisible pixel-perturbation watermarks are provably removable** (Zhao et al., NeurIPS 2024, proceedings 10272bfd0371ef960ec557ed6c866058) — 98% removal on RivaGAN — and the NeurIPS 2024 "Erasing the Invisible" competition (An et al., OpenReview BeFjjyzWOJ) confirmed empirically that top-5 teams removed ≥89% of watermarks in both Black-box and Beige-box tracks across Gaussian Shading + StegaStamp. The **primitive-native byte gate is not merely red — it is theoretically defeated**. Any serious receipt program must combine (a) semantic/inversion-based watermark (Shallow Diffuse, NeurIPS 2025 Spotlight), (b) cryptographic C2PA v2.0 manifest hard-binding, and (c) a semantic/detector stack such as DF40 (NeurIPS 2024 D&B, proceedings 34239f60eca7ce9bee5280aaf81362d8).

### (ii) Best external buyer/grant/research audiences

- **Buyers:** Adobe (C2PA founder), Microsoft, Google (SynthID-deployed in Gemini, published in *Nature* Oct 2024 — Dathathri et al.), BBC R&D, NYT, Truepic, Reuters. Publisher side: AP, Getty.
- **Grants:** NIST CAISI CRADA (provenance measurement science — Adobe/Microsoft already consortium members); DARPA I2O FY2026 BAA HR001126S0001 (SemaFor successor line); EU Digital Europe DIGITAL-2026-BESTUSE Safer Internet Centres; HE CL4-2026-05-DIGITAL-EMERGING-02 Next-Gen AI Agents (provenance-by-default framing).
- **Research:** Meta FAIR VideoSeal team (Fernandez et al., arXiv:2412.09492, with WmForger accepted NeurIPS 2025 Spotlight); Google DeepMind SynthID team; Microsoft DCVC group (Jiahao Li, Bin Li, Yan Lu — DCVC-FM CVPR 2024, DCVC-RT CVPR 2025).

### (iii) Exact gating logic for Phase 10

Phase 10 should be unblocked when **two of three** receipt-layer primitives are honestly green on a frozen test harness:

1. VideoSeal recovery bit-accuracy ≥0.95 after DCVC-FM re-encoding + H.266/VVC pass;
2. Shallow Diffuse detection AUC ≥0.90 on a frozen 1k-sample DF40 subset;
3. C2PA v2.0 manifest hard-bind verification at 100% on the same frozen set with at least one production trust-list anchor (Adobe / Microsoft / Leica).

This **re-scopes** the original primitive-native byte gate: under NeurIPS 2024 evidence, requiring a single-primitive byte gate is equivalent to requiring something the field has shown is theoretically defeatable; requiring 2-of-3 under the triple-lock is both defensible and achievable.

### (iv) Best next phase to insert if receipt wedge wins

**Insert a "Phase 10.5: Codec-Invariant Receipt Benchmark."** Publish a continuously updated leaderboard on DF40 + Panda-70M + LVD-2M measuring receipt survival after DCVC-FM / DCVC-RT / H.266 re-encoding and after NFPA-style next-frame-prediction attacks (NeurIPS 2025 poster). This is the neutral venue equivalent of GIFT-Eval for provenance; it positions ZPE-Video as the reference measurer, not the reference codec.

### (v) Ranked 3-step action plan with kill/hold conditions

1. **Ship VideoSeal + C2PA v2.0 manifest writer as the default receipt pipeline** (L, ~4 eng-weeks). Kill if VideoSeal bit-accuracy <0.70 after DCVC-FM on a 500-video smoke test after 4 weeks.
2. **Add Shallow Diffuse semantic watermark as orthogonal second signal** (M, ~8 eng-weeks). Hold if forgery attacks (per Müller et al. arXiv:2412.03283 "Black-Box Forgery Attacks on Semantic Watermarks") show >30% forgery on our frozen key.
3. **Release Phase 10.5 Codec-Invariant Receipt Benchmark as a public leaderboard** (M, ~6 eng-weeks). Kill if no external submissions arrive within 90 days post-release — pivot to CRADA arrangement instead.

### (vi) NeurIPS 2024/25 citations — one-line relevance

- **SynthID-Text** (Dathathri et al., *Nature* Oct 2024, doi:10.1038/s41586-024-08025-4) — production-deployed LLM watermark via tournament sampling, template for cross-writer receipt anchor.
- **ROBIN** (Huang, Wu, Wang, NeurIPS 2024, proceedings 073c8584ef86bee26fe9d639ec648e28) — adversarial hiding-prompt survives DDIM inversion; reference for cross-editor persistence.
- **Erasing the Invisible** (An et al., NeurIPS 2024 Competition Track, OpenReview BeFjjyzWOJ) — empirical ceiling of invisible image watermarks; evidence for triple-lock design.
- **NVRC** (Kwan et al., NeurIPS 2024) — first INR video codec to beat VTM-RA; receipts must survive INR re-encoding.
- **Shallow Diffuse** (NeurIPS 2025 Spotlight) — null-space semantic watermark, next-gen primitive.

### Re-scope argument

The current brief treats the "primitive-native byte gate" as a hard gate. NeurIPS 2024 evidence proves this gate cannot be closed with any single primitive; insisting on it indefinitely-parks a live commercial opportunity. Re-scope to a **triple-lock receipt gate** (VideoSeal + Shallow Diffuse + C2PA) that is both defensible and achievable.

### Engineering augmentation

**Build:** `receipt-core` — a verifier that ingests a video and returns a dense receipt: {videoseal_bits, shallow_diffuse_logit, c2pa_manifest_hash, trust_list_anchor}. **Why:** single integration point for any publisher; positions ZPE-Video as the de-facto EU AI Act Article 50 compliance layer for video. **Complexity:** M (~12 eng-weeks including DCVC-FM integration).

