## ZPE-Neuro — deterministic extracellular spike-event encoding

### (i) Best next breadth target

**IBL Brain-Wide Map** (International Brain Laboratory, *Nature* 645:177–191, 2025, doi:10.1038/s41586-025-09235-0). 621,733 neurons across 699 Neuropixels probes / 139 mice / 279 brain areas — this is the scale at which NeurIPS 2024/25 foundation models (MtM, NEDS, NEMO, POYO+) are trained and evaluated. DANDI 000034 (Marques-Smith rat cortex) is fine as a drift unit test but is **not frontier-scale**. Secondary target: DANDI 000957 (Neuropixels Ultra, Ye et al., *Neuron* 2025) for cell-type-diagnostic waveform experiments.

### (ii) Best blind-clone/replay strategy

Use the **FALCON benchmark harness** (Karpowicz et al., NeurIPS 2024 D&B, OpenReview FN02v4nD8y; bioRxiv 10.1101/2024.09.15.613126) as the blind-clone surface. FALCON defines few-shot decoding across 5 datasets (H1/M1/M2/H2/B1) with an EvalAI leaderboard — this is the community-standard blind evaluation for neural decoders. ZPE-Neuro can publish a deterministic-encoder reproducibility harness that wraps FALCON's held-out-day evaluation, making the replay both rigorous and externally auditable.

### (iii) Most credible grant/commercial framing

**Grant (primary):** NIH BRAIN RFA-DA-27-004 Theories/Models/Methods for Complex Brain Data (R01); RFA-DA-27-005 Data Archives (U24) for DANDI-adjacent infrastructure. ARPA-H Health Science Futures ISO for BCI-resilience framing. UK: ARIA Precision Neurotechnologies (seed rolling, ≤£500k, Scalable Neural Interfaces opportunity space). EU: ERC Starting Grant. APAC: India ANRF AI-SE Bio/Life Sciences program with DBT.

**Commercial:** Neuralink / Paradromics / Blackrock Neurotech / Synchron — all need deterministic encodings of their device streams for FDA IDE/510(k) submissions. IBL consortium members as research partners.

### (iv) Sharpest narrow wedge

**Deterministic FALCON-harness-compatible spike-event codec with replay guarantees across Kilosort4 version boundaries.** The sorting step introduces non-determinism; wrapping Kilosort4 (Pachitariu et al., *Nature Methods* 2024, doi:10.1038/s41592-024-02232-7) + DARTsort (Boussard et al.) in a byte-stable envelope with pinned random seeds and versioned templates is a real engineering contribution that no published foundation model provides.

### (v) Ranked 3-step action plan with kill/park conditions

1. **Pull a 50-session curated subset of IBL BWM via ONE-api; align deterministic encoder to MtM / FALCON protocols** (M, ~8 eng-weeks). Park if ONE-api licensing + data-access review exceeds 6 weeks.
2. **Publish blind-clone authority replay pack on DANDI 000034 + IBL subset using the FALCON harness** (L, ~4 eng-weeks). Kill if co-smoothing baseline cannot hit Neural Latents Benchmark parity (Pei et al., NBDT 2021) after 6 weeks.
3. **Add NEMO-style (Yu et al., ICLR 2025) ACG + multi-channel template triplet channels for cell-type retrieval at no extra commercialization cost** (M, ~10 eng-weeks). Kill if classification AUC on NP Ultra opto-tagged set <0.70 after 4 weeks.

**Park condition:** if IBL BWM data-access review exceeds 10 weeks and no commercial LOI arrives from Neuralink/Paradromics/Blackrock, park ZPE-Neuro at deterministic DANDI 000034 closure and redirect to ZPE-Bio (higher clinical-path asymmetry).

### (vi) NeurIPS 2024/25 citations

- **MtM / "Universal Translator"** (Zhang et al., NeurIPS 2024, arXiv:2407.14668, OpenReview nRRJsDahEg) — multi-task masking on IBL repeated-site; reference training recipe.
- **Brain-JEPA** (Dong et al., NeurIPS 2024 Spotlight, arXiv:2409.19407) — gradient positioning + spatiotemporal masking; methodologically central.
- **LDNS** (Kapoor et al., NeurIPS 2024 Spotlight, arXiv:2407.08751, OpenReview ZX6CEo1Wtv) — S4 + latent diffusion for spikes; reference generative baseline.
- **FALCON** (Karpowicz et al., NeurIPS 2024 D&B, OpenReview FN02v4nD8y) — the blind-clone benchmark to adopt.
- **Neuroformer** (Antoniades et al., ICLR 2024, arXiv:2311.00136) — GPT on (neuron-id, Δt) tokens.

### Re-scope argument

Current scope "DANDI 000034 + bounded IBL" undersells what the lane can do. IBL BWM (Nature 2025) is the frontier corpus and is freely accessible via ONE-api; keeping scope bounded to 000034 makes ZPE-Neuro look like a toy relative to MtM/NEDS/NEMO. Re-scope to **IBL BWM primary, DANDI 000034 as drift/probe unit test**.

### Engineering augmentation

**Build:** `spike-codec-falcon` — deterministic encoder that consumes Kilosort4+DARTsort output, emits a FALCON-compatible token stream, and ships with a byte-stable replay harness. **Why:** unlocks NIH BRAIN R01 (FALCON compatibility is grant-legible); positions against Neuralink/Paradromics FDA submissions. **Complexity:** M (~12 eng-weeks).

