## ZPE-Mocap — motion capture retrieval/indexing

### (i) Strongest retrieval/indexing wedge

**Cross-corpus motion retrieval across HumanML3D ↔ Motion-X++ ↔ AMASS with a TMR/SGAR-grade dual encoder + RVQ tokenization head.** The NeurIPS 2025 papers make this decisive: **SGAR** (NeurIPS 2025 main, neurips.cc/virtual/2025/loc/san-diego/poster/119557) provides LLM-decomposed body-part alignment for fine-grained motion-text retrieval on three benchmarks; **VimoRAG** (NeurIPS 2025) shows retrieval-augmented motion generation is a live research program with Gemini Motion Video Retriever. Synthetic P@10=1.0 is not a credible claim — it must be replaced by cross-corpus median rank on published datasets.

### (ii) Best next real-data benchmark or corpus expansion

**Motion-X++** (Zhang et al., arXiv:2501.05098) — 19.5M SMPL-X frames, 120.5K sequences, 80.8K RGB videos, 45.3K audios. It is the 2025 successor to Motion-X (NeurIPS 2023 D&B) and is the single best expansion for cross-corpus retrieval. Secondary: **SnapMoGen** (Guo et al., NeurIPS 2025, arXiv:2507.09122) with 20K clips + ~48-word descriptions for long-prompt retrieval. Third: cross-embodiment via DROID (Khazatsky et al., RSS 2024, arXiv:2403.12945) and Open-X Embodiment to bridge into robotics-retrieval commercial wedge.

### (iii) Best commercial and grant story under current truth

**Commercial:** humanoid retargeting-as-a-service for Unitree / Figure / 1X / Agility / Disney, using the 19-DoF Unitree H1 as the industry retargeting target (per ExBody, OmniH2O, HOVER, ASAP, SONIC). ZPE-Mocap's compressed retrieval index sits upstream of their control stacks.

