**Evidence-picked thesis:** *"Deterministic, compressed-searchable, provenance-grade codec substrate for regulated multi-modal data, anchored in NeurIPS-2024/25 tokenization and retrieval primitives."*

This wins over the alternatives by construction, not by preference:

- *"Cross-modal tokenization + retrieval as a substrate for world models"* is narrower — it excludes the provenance/audit DNA that ZPE-Video, ZPE-Bio, and ZPE-FT have independently developed, and which matches the 2024-2026 regulatory wave (EU AI Act Article 50, FDA PCCP Dec 2024, tri-national PCCP principles Aug 2025, NIST AI 100-4).
- *"Provenance-grade codec layer for the AI Act era"* is narrower in the opposite direction — it excludes the retrieval and compression DNA that ZPE-Prosody, ZPE-Mocap, ZPE-Geo, ZPE-FT have developed.
- *"Code-physics substrate for compressed-representation science across modalities"* is too abstract to be grant-legible.

The winning thesis uniquely captures all three portfolio-DNA strands — determinism + compression+retrieval + provenance — and all three align with frontier primitives validated at NeurIPS 2024/25: tokenization (OmniTokenizer, Mimi, MoMask/MoGenTS, Kronos, UniTraj, ink-tokens), compressed retrieval (RaBitQ, SOAR, LoRANN, TMR/SGAR, VimoRAG), and provenance/replay (VideoSeal, SynthID, C2PA v2.0, FALCON, FDA PCCP). The same three primitives recur across all ten lanes — that recurrence **is** the unifying thesis.

### (b) Three highest-asymmetry cross-lane moves

**Move 1 — Shared deterministic replay harness across Neuro + Bio + Video + Mocap.** FALCON (NeurIPS 2024 D&B), FDA PCCP (Dec 2024), DIAMOND-style world-model replay (NeurIPS 2024 Spotlight), and TMR-style motion retrieval all require the same underlying primitive: byte-stable replay of a tokenized stream with pinned model weights and deterministic sampling. ZPE-Neuro's `spike-codec-falcon`, ZPE-Bio's `ecg-pccp-replay`, ZPE-Video's `receipt-core`, and ZPE-Mocap's `mocap-rvq-tmr` should share a single `zpe-replay-core` substrate. Only possible because all four lanes already exist with independent traction; building from scratch this abstraction would take 6+ months, but abstracting from four live lanes takes ~4 eng-weeks.

**Move 2 — Shared compressed-search index substrate across Prosody + Mocap + Geo + FT + Ink.** All five lanes face the same retrieval problem: CPU-first ANN over billions of high-dimensional tokens with replay-deterministic indexing. RaBitQ (SIGMOD 2024) + SOAR (NeurIPS 2023) + LoRANN (NeurIPS 2024) + PGM++ (2024) + DiskANN cover the backbone. A single `zpe-index-core` library (Rust + SIMD, with Python/Swift/C# bindings following ZPE-Ink's cross-runtime discipline) would serve all five lanes. Asymmetry: a single investment in one team produces retrieval for five lanes, with identical correctness guarantees and identical benchmark story.

**Move 3 — Shared provenance/receipt layer across Video + Ink + IoT + Bio + Geo.** EU AI Act Article 50, C2PA v2.0, FDA PCCP, SEC CAT, IMO AIS guidelines A.1106(29), and NIST AI 100-4 all demand the same thing: signed, verifiable, replay-auditable provenance over codec outputs. ZPE-Video's `receipt-core` (VideoSeal ⊕ Shallow Diffuse ⊕ C2PA) generalizes directly to: ECG receipts under PCCP (ZPE-Bio), sensor-stream receipts under MLCommons Tiny (ZPE-IoT), AIS receipts under IMO (ZPE-Geo), ink-stroke receipts for educational/legal contexts (ZPE-Ink). A single `zpe-receipt-core` layer turns the five lanes into a coherent regulatory-ready offering.

